  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "n5r82P4cyguSRYC9JJOs6cqd4zM=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:18:37.560Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Sync does not keep a cursor per document. Operations are grouped into **collections**, and a collection has one cursor over the flattened stream of every operation belonging to it:\n\n```ts\nconst collectionId = `drive.${branch}.${driveId}`;\n```\n\nWhen a document is added to a drive it **joins the drive's collection**, and from then on its operations appear in that collection's stream. The cursor advances through `ordinal` values from the operation index, which is exactly why the index assigns a global ordinal in the first place \u2014 per-scope `index` values could not order a multi-document stream.\n\nThe practical consequence: sync progress for a drive with 900 documents is one number, and a new document does not add a cursor to maintain. Membership is stored in `document_collections`.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/reactor/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 Synchronization \u203a Collection-Based Sync\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:18:37.560Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:18:37.560Z"
    }
  },
  {
    "index": 4,
    "hash": "",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:20:56.503Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "ADD_RELATIONSHIP",
      "input": {
        "metadata": {
          "reason": "Cursors are tracked in ordinals, and ordinals are local to a reactor \u2014 which is what makes the poll exchange's two frames of reference necessary",
          "confidence": "grounded"
        },
        "sourceId": "562d84eb-ef1d-40b7-81b0-b6b7438544e1",
        "targetId": "936ddc46-3b5a-40d1-b69f-6a3f6c3c6b8f",
